  {
    question: 'What is trail magic?',
    answer: 'Trail magic is an unexpected act of kindness or generosity experienced along a long-distance trail. On the A.T., that might mean a thoughtful conversation, a ride into town, water offered in person, or help that arrives at exactly the right moment. The Appalachian Trail Conservancy also cautions that trail magic should protect the Trail and should not make hikers feel like a captive audience. [1]'
  },
